      "content": "The relationship makes sense, but we're seeing some really weird, erratic spikes in the salinity data that don't align with the temperature drops. It almost looks like sensor noise or some kind of intermittent malfunction in the AUV's conductivity cell. How should I distinguish between actual localized salinity anomalies and just bad instrument readings?",
